window.MG_LAZY_DATA["data/lazy/resources/security-v27-096-139a04199010f875.json"]={sha256:"139a04199010f875fbf4257f59804cc3454d545d24f27e5ca677dda2dba49105",value:{"sources":[{"id":"v27-case-8e60629cd90d098c","url":"https://sre.google/workbook/postmortem-culture/","title":"Google SRE Workbook: postmortem culture","titleEn":"Google SRE Workbook: postmortem culture","publisher":"Google","scope":"查證具名案例與原理背景。課內數值、故障資料與判準為原創教學假設；請勿當作廠商規格或操作程序。","scopeEn":"Establish named case and principle context. Numbers, fault data, and criteria are original teaching assumptions, not manufacturer specifications or operating procedures."}],"media":{"courses":[{"courseId":"security-v27-096","videos":[],"guides":[]}]},"related":{"courses":[{"courseId":"security-v27-096","related":[{"id":"security-v27-097","referenceUrls":["https://www.cisa.gov/resources-tools/services/cisa-tabletop-exercise-packages"],"title":"CISA CTEP：分支情境矩陣與未演練決策路徑","titleEn":"CISA CTEP: scenario-branch matrices and unexercised decision paths","why":"用兩課的可觀察驗收條件比較模型邊界：交付stratified-results.csv、fixed-weights.json、before-after-report.md與scenario-changes.csv，讓審查者能直接重算50%與82%。","whyEn":"Compare model boundaries using observable acceptance criteria: Deliver stratified-results.csv, fixed-weights.json, before-after-report.md and scenario-changes.csv. Reviewers must reproduce both 50% and 82% and identify the precise composition change responsible for their difference.","difference":"將證據可用、主要聯絡角色可用、備份驗證通過三個二元因素列出全部組合，為每組寫預期決策、停止條件與觀察證據。","differenceEn":"Enumerate all combinations of three binary factors: evidence availability, primary-contact availability and backup-verification success. Define expected decisions, stop conditions and observable evidence for each combination.","transfer":"保留單位與邊界條件，僅轉移可證明相容的驗證方法。","transferEn":"Retain units and boundary conditions; transfer only demonstrably compatible verification methods.","practice":["SRE事後檢討要求可追蹤的改進；此課分層統計是原創驗證方法，不是Google規定的評分公式，也不能單靠前後對照排除所有混淆。 本課所有數值、事件與系統狀態均為原創合成資料；只在本機檔案與授權隔離練習中處理，不接觸生產設備或他人資料。 改善前容易100件成功90、困難100件成功10；改善後容易900成功810、困難100成功10。層內成功率皆維持90%與10%。 前總成功100/200=50%，後820/1000=82%；以各50%固定權重標準化，前後皆(90%+10%)/2=50%。","CISA CTEP提供可調整的目標、情境與討論材料；本課8格矩陣是自行設計的覆蓋模型，不代表CISA認證或完整風險集合。 本課所有數值、事件與系統狀態均為原創合成資料；只在本機檔案與授權隔離練習中處理，不接觸生產設備或他人資料。 三個二元因素共2×2×2=8格；第一輪有4個不同組合留下決策證據，另重複其中一格3次，不算新增覆蓋。 不同組合覆蓋4/8=50%，不是7/8；重複次數可測熟練或一致性，但不等於探索新決策路徑。","比較兩個模型的輸入、誤差與驗收條件，記錄不能沿用的假設。"],"practiceEn":["SRE postmortem practice supports accountable improvement. The stratified calculation is an original verification method, not a prescribed Google scoring formula; before/after comparison alone cannot eliminate all confounding. Every quantity, event and system state below is original synthetic teaching data. Work only on local files or an explicitly authorized isolated lab, without production access or other people’s data. Before the change, easy cases have ninety successes out of 100 and hard cases ten out of 100. Afterward, easy cases have 810 out of 900 and hard cases ten out of 100. Pooled success rises from 100/200=50% to 820/1000=82%. Standardizing both periods to equal stratum weights gives (90%+10%)/2=50% in each period.","CISA CTEP provides customizable objectives, scenarios and discussion materials. The eight-cell matrix is an original coverage model, not a CISA certification or an exhaustive inventory of operational risks. Every quantity, event and system state below is original synthetic teaching data. Work only on local files or an explicitly authorized isolated lab, without production access or other people’s data. Three binary factors produce 2×2×2=8 cells. The first round documents decisions for four distinct combinations; three additional repeats of one existing combination add no new branch coverage. Distinct-combination coverage is 4/8=50%, not 7/8. Repetition can assess consistency or practice, but it does not explore a previously untested decision branch.","Compare inputs, errors, and criteria; document assumptions that cannot be transferred."]},{"id":"security-v27-006","referenceUrls":["https://docs.cloud.google.com/iam/docs/best-practices-for-using-workload-identity-federation"],"title":"Google WIF：共享 issuer 的租戶隔離","titleEn":"Google WIF: tenant isolation under a shared issuer","why":"用兩課的可觀察驗收條件比較模型邊界：交付stratified-results.csv、fixed-weights.json、before-after-report.md與scenario-changes.csv，讓審查者能直接重算50%與82%。","whyEn":"Compare model boundaries using observable acceptance criteria: Deliver stratified-results.csv, fixed-weights.json, before-after-report.md and scenario-changes.csv. Reviewers must reproduce both 50% and 82% and identify the precise composition change responsible for their difference.","difference":"製作A、B兩個虛構組織各八筆token描述，讓兩邊都有build角色；列issuer、organization ID、repository ID與映射subject，找出僅以角色名映射的碰撞。","differenceEn":"Create eight token descriptors for each of fictional organizations A and B, both containing a build role. Tabulate issuer, organization ID, repository ID and mapped subject to expose role-name-only collisions.","transfer":"保留單位與邊界條件，僅轉移可證明相容的驗證方法。","transferEn":"Retain units and boundary conditions; transfer only demonstrably compatible verification methods.","practice":["SRE事後檢討要求可追蹤的改進；此課分層統計是原創驗證方法，不是Google規定的評分公式，也不能單靠前後對照排除所有混淆。 本課所有數值、事件與系統狀態均為原創合成資料；只在本機檔案與授權隔離練習中處理，不接觸生產設備或他人資料。 改善前容易100件成功90、困難100件成功10；改善後容易900成功810、困難100成功10。層內成功率皆維持90%與10%。 前總成功100/200=50%，後820/1000=82%；以各50%固定權重標準化，前後皆(90%+10%)/2=50%。","映射身分與授權條件是不同層次；不可因簽章來自共同issuer就信任其所有租戶。組織識別使用固定測試ID，顯示名稱只作說明。 共16筆，單看共同issuer全數符合；加上A組織條件後8筆符合，再加受控repository條件只剩5筆。 組織限定後8/16×100=50%；再限定repository後5/16×100=31.25%。縮小可用集合不是偵測率或服務可用性量測。","比較兩個模型的輸入、誤差與驗收條件，記錄不能沿用的假設。"],"practiceEn":["SRE postmortem practice supports accountable improvement. The stratified calculation is an original verification method, not a prescribed Google scoring formula; before/after comparison alone cannot eliminate all confounding. Every quantity, event and system state below is original synthetic teaching data. Work only on local files or an explicitly authorized isolated lab, without production access or other people’s data. Before the change, easy cases have ninety successes out of 100 and hard cases ten out of 100. Afterward, easy cases have 810 out of 900 and hard cases ten out of 100. Pooled success rises from 100/200=50% to 820/1000=82%. Standardizing both periods to equal stratum weights gives (90%+10%)/2=50% in each period.","Identity mapping and authorization conditions are distinct layers. Trusting a shared issuer's signature does not authorize every tenant. Use fixed fictional organization IDs; display names are explanatory metadata, not the sole trust anchor. All 16 fixtures match the common issuer. Requiring organization A leaves eight; additionally requiring the approved repository leaves five. Every count refers to this enumerated synthetic set. Organization restriction gives 8/16×100=50%; adding repository restriction gives 5/16×100=31.25%. This reduced eligible set is neither a detection rate nor a measured service-availability figure.","Compare inputs, errors, and criteria; document assumptions that cannot be transferred."]}],"references":[{"id":"v27-case-b9fc9baa8f876204","url":"https://www.cisa.gov/resources-tools/services/cisa-tabletop-exercise-packages","title":"CISA Cybersecurity Tabletop Exercise Tips","titleEn":"CISA Cybersecurity Tabletop Exercise Tips","publisher":"CISA","scope":"查證具名案例與原理背景。課內數值、故障資料與判準為原創教學假設；請勿當作廠商規格或操作程序。","scopeEn":"Establish named case and principle context. Numbers, fault data, and criteria are original teaching assumptions, not manufacturer specifications or operating procedures."},{"id":"v27-case-9e49b6e057aee700","url":"https://docs.cloud.google.com/iam/docs/best-practices-for-using-workload-identity-federation","title":"Best practices for Workload Identity Federation","titleEn":"Best practices for Workload Identity Federation","publisher":"Google Cloud","scope":"查證具名案例與原理背景。課內數值、故障資料與判準為原創教學假設；請勿當作廠商規格或操作程序。","scopeEn":"Establish named case and principle context. Numbers, fault data, and criteria are original teaching assumptions, not manufacturer specifications or operating procedures."}],"overview":"比較相鄰案例與另一組案例的模型、可量測結果及可轉移的驗證方法。","overviewEn":"Compare neighboring and cross-group cases by model, measurable outcome, and transferable verification method."}]},"places":{"courses":[]},"vendors":{"courses":[],"vendors":[]}}};
